  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS Ukraine &#x2013; hydrological expertise</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UN Environment Programme (UNEP) has requested the assistance of the DRRS programme to provide hydrological expertise for the Environmental Impact Assessment after the Kakhovka Dam breach in Ukraine.On the 6th of June 2023, a critical part of the infrastructure in southern Ukraine, the Kakhovka Dam, was breached. A vast amount of water was unleashed downstream along the Dnipro river.Based on the available information, the following expertise is required by UNEP: 1.	Hydrology expertise, to consider the impacts of event. 2.	Hydrology expertise, to consider future scenarios.</narrative>
  </description>
